.TH THERMAL-ENGINE 8 2026-09-21 "Linux 7.0.9" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
thermal\-engine \- report thermal zone state and thermal events from the kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B \%thermal\-engine
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR level ]
.br
.B \%thermal\-engine \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B \%thermal\-engine
is a thermal monitoring program built on
.B libthermal
and the kernel's thermal generic netlink family,
.BR thermal .
It subscribes to the family's
.B event
multicast group and reports what the kernel's thermal framework does.
.PP
At startup it:
.IP 1. 4
discovers the thermal zones and reads each zone's trip points,
thresholds and governor;
.IP 2. 4
for each zone, removes all existing thresholds and then adds five
thresholds, at 43000, 49000, 55000, 57000 and 65000 millidegrees Celsius,
each reported when crossed in either direction;
.IP 3. 4
for each zone, prints its name and identifier, its trip points
(identifier, type, temperature and hysteresis),
the thresholds read in step 1,
its current temperature and its governor.
.PP
It then prints
\(dqWaiting for thermal events ...\(dq
and prints a message for each event the kernel sends:
a thermal zone created, deleted, enabled or disabled;
a trip point crossed upwards or downwards, added, deleted or changed;
a cooling device added, deleted or changing state;
a zone's governor changed;
and a threshold added, deleted, flushed, or crossed upwards or downwards.
.PP
Temperatures are printed as the kernel reports them,
in millidegrees Celsius.
Trip types and threshold directions are printed as numbers.
A threshold direction is a bit mask in which 1 means upwards and 2 means
downwards.
.PP
Messages are written to standard output, or to
.BR syslog (3)
with
.BR \-s .
.B \%thermal\-engine
runs until it is killed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Detach from the controlling terminal and run in the background, using
.BR daemon (3).
The working directory is changed to
.I /
and standard input, standard output and standard error are redirected to
.IR /dev/null ,
so without
.B \-s
all messages are discarded.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-syslog
Send messages to
.BR syslog (3),
with facility
.B LOG_USER
and the base name of the program as identity,
instead of to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-loglevel " \fIlevel\fP"
Set the lowest priority of messages passed to
.BR syslog (3).
.I level
is one of
.BR EMERG ,
.BR ALERT ,
.BR CRITICAL ,
.BR ERROR ,
.BR WARN ,
.BR NOTICE ,
.BR INFO ,
or
.BR DEBUG ,
in upper case.
Any other value selects
.BR DEBUG .
The default is
.BR INFO .
The level takes effect only together with
.BR \-s ;
messages written to standard output are not filtered.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage message to standard output and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The usage message was printed.
.TP
.B 1
An invalid option was given, or an option argument was missing.
.TP
.B 2
.BR daemon (3)
failed.
.TP
.B 3
The logging facility could not be initialised.
.TP
.B 4
The thermal library could not be initialised,
or no thermal zone could be discovered.
.TP
.B 6
The event loop could not be set up or failed.
.SH NOTES
The kernel must be built with
.B \%CONFIG_THERMAL_NETLINK
to provide the thermal netlink interface.
.PP
The thresholds set at startup replace any thresholds already configured
on each zone, and remain in place after
.B \%thermal\-engine
exits.
The kernel accepts the commands that remove and add thresholds only from a
caller with
.BR CAP_SYS_ADMIN ,
which Peios maps to
.BR SeTcbPrivilege .
Without it,
.B \%thermal\-engine
logs
\(dqFailed to flush all previous thresholds\(dq
for each zone and continues without setting thresholds.
.PP
Errors are reported through the same channel as other messages.
An invalid option or a failure of
.B \-d
occurs before logging is set up, so
.B \%thermal\-engine
prints no message of its own for it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daemon (3),
.BR syslog (3)
.PP
The thermal sysfs interface, including temperature units, is described in
the Linux kernel source in
.PP
.I \%Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs\-class\-thermal
.br
.I \%Documentation/driver\-api/thermal/sysfs\-api.rst
